# Open work

Every row of every tracker's **Open** table, read from the trackers under
`doc/status/`: its state, the bold lead sentence that names the work, and the
tracker that owns it. A row's notes, its references, and what unblocks a
`blocked` row stay in the tracker, one click away; this view only says where
the work is.

This is a generated view, not a tracker: refresh it with the command in
[the status README](README.md), and never edit an output by hand. A row reaches
this view only when it starts with one of the board's states and a bold lead,
which is the form [the README](README.md) asks every Open row to take.

```hql#eval id=rows hidden
import regex

// An Open row: its state, the work it names, and the tracker it comes from.
type OpenRow { state : String, work : String, tracker : String }

// The text of a tracker's `## Open` section, up to the next heading.
fn open_section(body: String) : String =
    regex.find(body, "(?s)\\n## Open\\n.*?(\\n## |\\z)").unwrap_or("")

// The Open rows of one tracker.
fn rows_of(c: Card) : Seq<OpenRow> =
    regex.find_all(open_section(c.body),
        "(?m)^\\| (doing|todo|blocked|backlog|parked) \\| \\*\\*[^*]+\\*\\*")
    | map(line => OpenRow(
        state = regex.find(line, "^\\| [a-z]+").map(s => regex.replace_first(s, "^\\| ", "")).unwrap_or(""),
        work = regex.replace_first(regex.replace_first(line, "^\\| [a-z]+ \\| \\*\\*", ""), "\\*\\*$", ""),
        tracker = "[" + c.name + "](" + c.name + ".hmd)",
      ))

cards
| filter(c => regex.is_match(c.path, "^status/[a-z-]+\\.hmd$")
    and not regex.is_match(c.path, "^status/(kanban|open|proposals)\\.hmd$"))
| sort(by = c => c.path)
| flat_map(c => rows_of(c))
```

## By state

The number of open rows in each state, across every tracker: the states of
the board, in the order this view lists them.

```hql#eval
["doing", "todo", "blocked", "backlog", "parked"]
| map(s => { state: s, rows: rows | filter(r => r.state == s) | size })
| Table(columns = ["state", "rows"])
| format(as = Markdown)
```
<!-- hql:output hash=2d3c7edd4b79 status=ok -->
| state   | rows |
| ------- | ---- |
| doing   | 2    |
| todo    | 27   |
| blocked | 5    |
| backlog | 11   |
| parked  | 3    |
<!-- /hql:output -->

## Rows

Every open row, `doing` first, then `todo`, `blocked`, `backlog` and
`parked`, and by tracker within each state.

```hql#eval
["doing", "todo", "blocked", "backlog", "parked"]
| flat_map(s => rows | filter(r => r.state == s))
| map(r => { state: r.state, work: r.work, tracker: r.tracker })
| Table(columns = ["state", "work", "tracker"])
| format(as = Markdown)
```
